{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261113T015214Z_dev-05_flat_3cc3", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not give a detection significance (in σ or as a test statistic) for the GCE in its 17.7-year analysis. It says only that the fitted GCE flux stays nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models, so a GCE component persists. It adds that this 'alone does not establish its statistical significance'. It also says the Δ(−2lnL) differences between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The numbers it does report are DM-fit χ² values (e.g. χ²_min=27.50 for 12 dof in the bb̄ channel) and Δ(−2lnL) values comparing diffuse models relative to Model X (72.1 for the next-best model, LIII). None of these is a GCE detection significance.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}]}, "turns": 11, "seconds": 20.121, "tool_calls": 10, "tool_result_chars": 511789, "input_tokens": 1392361, "output_tokens": 1154, "parser_versions": ["3"], "ended_at": "2026-11-13T01:52:34+00:00"}
